HST Office: ribbon groups are as wide as their controls, with no empty room beside them.

A group whose caption was wider than its controls looked like it had empty slots: the caption stretched
the group's columns (VclGrid shares a wide caption's extra width out to the columns), the toolboxes filled
the stretched columns and drew their buttons from the left, and the extra room stayed empty on their
right. The default collapse ladder (every tab but Home) made it worse: it turned buttons into bare icons
to save a few pixels (Insert's Extensions and Comments became a small icon under a long caption), and its
last step could free far more room than was missing, which stayed empty while other groups had shrunk.

- VclGrid (off by default, set_hst_centre_spanned): a ribbon group's caption (a label, or the box of a
  label and the group's launcher, in the last row) no longer stretches the columns it spans; they keep
  their width and sit centred under it, and only the caption gets the extra room.
  get_hst_caption_room tells how much wider the caption is than the controls.
- PriorityMergedHBox turns it on for its groups.
- A group of one large command keeps it large with its label at every state (HstRibbonLadder.cxx),
  as Paste already did.
- Tabs without a ladder of their own: a group shrinks to medium (small icons with labels), then to its
  button "caption ▾" (which opens the group at full size, as on Home), then folds into the chevron.
  Small (labels dropped) is no rung there, nor is a step that saves less than 24 px (scaled) or no more
  room than the caption leaves empty. After the ladder, collapsed groups come back and shrunk groups grow
  back, latest first, into the largest state that still fits the room left. The Home tabs' authored
  ladders are unchanged.
- The single small buttons of Writer's and Slides' Media group and Sheets' Themes group are large
  buttons, as the other one-button groups.

